    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45691" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφετ-μή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφίημι</span>) poet. word, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>command, behest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.249
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ὤτρυνεν ἐφετμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.299
				</span></i>
			: freq. in pl., <i>behests</i>, esp. of the gods or one's
			parents, <i><span class="en">
				5.508
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				3.11
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θέτις δ᾽ οὐ λήθετ᾽ ἐφετμέων παιδὸς
					ἑοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.495
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				300
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				634
			</span></i>; <i>demands, prayers</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				6(5).18
			</span></i>.</div>
